# Patterns that HARD-DENY a write when the target file already exists.
# Applies to Write/Edit tools and to inferred Bash write targets (redirects,
# tee, sed -i, mv/cp dest). Creating an absent file still falls through to the
# ask-before-write prompt — this list only blocks overwrite/replace of an
# existing file. Escape hatch: run the command yourself with the `!` shell
# prefix, which bypasses the hook entirely.
#
# Same pattern shapes and !pattern negation as ask-before-write.

# Protect ONLY the literal .env — dev .env must never be clobbered by copying
# TEST.env / .env.CI over it. A bare basename ".env" also matches ".env.local",
# ".env.CI" etc. (basename.startsWith(".env.")), so negate the dotted variants:
# those are safe to (re)write.
.env
!.env.*
